IMPORT prelude

-- Pension Fund Act 1995 (Singapore) -- what goes into the Pension Fund (s 4), what may come out of it and on whose authority
-- (ss 6, 7, 10), who bears a shortfall (s 8), transfers of surplus by warrant (s 9), the financial year (s 12(2)), the periodic and
-- triggered actuarial examinations (s 13), and the Schedule of written laws whose benefits the Fund pays.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PFA1995.txt. The deposit says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is 4/2021 (Schedule item 13).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The Act is short (15 sections and a Schedule) and
-- institutional: it creates a Government fund and says what may be paid into and out of it. Nearly all of it with decision content
-- is encoded. Not encoded: s 3 (establishment), s 5 (investment, which points to s 7 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966, not read),
-- s 11 (accounts), s 12(1) (audit by the Auditor-General), s 14 (Financial Procedure Act applies), s 15 (regulations), the meaning
-- of "prescribed superannuation scheme" (left to regulations, none retrieved), and the content of any law in the Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pension Fund Act 1995 -- the Pension Fund`

§§ `4 -- moneys paid in`

-- s 4(1): there must be paid in (a) sums appropriated from the Consolidated Fund and authorised by written law "to enable the Pension
-- Fund to meet the liabilities of the Pension Fund"; (b) revenues allocated by written law; (c) the net income from authorised
-- investments. (2): net income is "the amount ascertained by adding to, or deducting from, the income received from investments ...
-- any profit derived or loss sustained (as the case may be) from the realisation of the investments".
GIVEN `income received` IS A NUMBER, `profit on realisation` IS A NUMBER, `loss on realisation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `net income from investments` IS
    `income received` + `profit on realisation` - `loss on realisation`

§§ `The Schedule -- written laws whose benefits the Fund pays`

-- The Schedule (ss 6 and 13(2)) lists 13 items, among them: 2. Civil List and Gratuity Act 1970; 6. Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978;
-- 7. Pensions Act 1956; 10. "Section 206(1) of the Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972"; 12. Widows' and Orphans' Pension Act 1904;
-- 13. Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 "or the Work Injury Compensation Act (Cap. 354, 2009 Revised Edition) repealed by that Act".
-- Item 10 names one subsection, not the whole Singapore Armed Forces Act. The Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001
-- appears in s 9(3) (as the home of the INVEST Fund) but not in the Schedule. s 6(2): the Minister may amend the Schedule by order in
-- the Gazette, so this list is only as current as the deposit.
DECLARE Law IS ONE OF
    `Civil List and Gratuity Act 1970`
    `Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978`
    `Pensions Act 1956`
    `Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 section 206(1)`
    `Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 another section`
    `Widows' and Orphans' Pension Act 1904`
    `Work Injury Compensation Act 2019`
    `the repealed Work Injury Compensation Act Cap 354`
    `Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001`
    `some other written law`

GIVEN `the law` IS A Law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972 another section` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `some other written law` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6, 7 and 10 -- moneys paid out`

-- s 6(1): moneys "may only be withdrawn and applied" to (a) a pension, gratuity, allowance or other like benefit under a law in the
-- Schedule to persons who have been in the public service in Singapore (or their legal personal representatives or dependants) on
-- death, superannuation, resignation, retirement or discharge; (b) a disability pension, injury allowance, gratuity or compensation
-- under a law in the Schedule to such persons "in respect of injuries received in and which are attributable to that service";
-- (c) an ex gratia sum or benefit "pursuant to a prescribed superannuation scheme"; (d) a gratuity on the death or retirement of
-- "members of the local staff of any diplomatic mission of Singapore"; (e) other expenses of granting an (a) or (b) benefit
-- "expressly provided by written law to be met out of the Pension Fund".
-- s 7: expenses of administration, investment and management "are charged on and payable out of the Fund".
-- s 10(1): moneys must not be withdrawn "unless they are charged on the Fund or authorised to be withdrawn under this Act".
-- (2): "A payment must not be made out of the Pension Fund unless the payment is authorised by the Minister."
-- s 2: "public service" includes service as an MP, in the Special Constabulary, as a volunteer in the SAF or SCDF, and other service
-- determined to be public service for the Pensions Act 1956. Here it is a single flag.
--
-- Note that (d) does not require the recipient to have been in the public service, nor a law in the Schedule: the local staff
-- gratuity stands alone. Paragraph (e) reaches only (a) and (b) benefits, not (c) or (d).
DECLARE Payment HAS
    `is a pension, gratuity or allowance on death, superannuation, resignation, retirement or discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a disability pension, injury allowance, gratuity or compensation for injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury was received in and is attributable to the service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is granted under a law in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has been in the public service in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is paid under a prescribed superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a gratuity on death or retirement of local staff of a Singapore diplomatic mission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is another expense of granting an (a) or (b) benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `written law expressly provides it is met out of the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an expense of administering, investing or managing the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is a section 6 purpose` IF
        (     `the payment`'s `is a pension, gratuity or allowance on death, superannuation, resignation, retirement or discharge`
          AND `the payment`'s `is granted under a law in the Schedule`
          AND `the payment`'s `the person has been in the public service in Singapore`)
    OR  (     `the payment`'s `is a disability pension, injury allowance, gratuity or compensation for injury`
          AND `the payment`'s `the injury was received in and is attributable to the service`
          AND `the payment`'s `is granted under a law in the Schedule`
          AND `the payment`'s `the person has been in the public service in Singapore`)
    OR  `the payment`'s `is paid under a prescribed superannuation scheme`
    OR  `the payment`'s `is a gratuity on death or retirement of local staff of a Singapore diplomatic mission`
    OR  (     `the payment`'s `is another expense of granting an (a) or (b) benefit`
          AND `the payment`'s `written law expressly provides it is met out of the Fund`)

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment may be made out of the Fund` IF
        (    `the payment is a section 6 purpose` `the payment`
          OR `the payment`'s `is an expense of administering, investing or managing the Fund`)
    AND `the payment`'s `is authorised by the Minister`

§§ `8 -- who bears a deficiency`

-- s 8(1): where the moneys in the Fund "are insufficient to pay any pension, gratuity, allowance, compensation or other like benefit
-- at the time when the payment becomes due, the deficiency is charged on and payable out of the Consolidated Fund".
-- (2): (1) "applies only to" a benefit for persons who have been in the public service in Singapore which "(a) prior to 1 April 1995,
-- was charged on the Consolidated Fund; or (b) is provided for under any written law enacted on or after 1 April 1995".
-- A benefit under a pre-1995 law that was not charged on the Consolidated Fund before 1 April 1995 falls outside the guarantee.
GIVEN `the Fund is insufficient when the payment falls due` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the benefit is for a person who has been in the public service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the benefit was charged on the Consolidated Fund before 1 April 1995` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the benefit is provided under a law enacted on or after 1 April 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deficiency is charged on the Consolidated Fund` IF
        `the Fund is insufficient when the payment falls due`
    AND `the benefit is for a person who has been in the public service`
    AND (    `the benefit was charged on the Consolidated Fund before 1 April 1995`
          OR `the benefit is provided under a law enacted on or after 1 April 1995`)

§§ `9 -- transfers out by warrant`

-- s 9: the Minister may "by warrant under his or her hand" authorise a transfer (1) to the Consolidated Fund of moneys "which, in the
-- opinion of the Minister, are not required to meet the liabilities of the Pension Fund"; (2) to the SAVER-Premium Fund (s 205B
-- Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972) of the value of the part of the Fund relating to servicemen who opted for the SAVER Plan or Premium
-- Plan; (3) to the INVEST Fund (s 12 Home Affairs Uniformed Services Superannuation Act 2001) of the value relating to officers who
-- opted for the INVEST Plan or for the Occupational Superannuation Scheme under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960.
-- The Act names no other destination.
DECLARE Destination IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the SAVER-Premium Fund`
    `the INVEST Fund`
    `any other fund`

GIVEN `the destination` IS A Destination,
      `made by warrant under the Minister's hand` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister is of the opinion the moneys are not required for the Fund's liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the amount is the value the Minister determines for the members who opted for the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer may be authorised` IF
    `made by warrant under the Minister's hand`
    AND CONSIDER `the destination`
        WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN `the Minister is of the opinion the moneys are not required for the Fund's liabilities`
        WHEN `the SAVER-Premium Fund` THEN `the amount is the value the Minister determines for the members who opted for the plan`
        WHEN `the INVEST Fund` THEN `the amount is the value the Minister determines for the members who opted for the plan`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `12(2) -- the financial year`

-- s 12(2): "the financial year of the Pension Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year".
-- Returned here as the calendar year in which the financial year begins.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the financial year begins in` IS
    IF `the month` >= 4 THEN `the year` ELSE `the year` - 1

§§ `13 -- examinations of the Fund`

-- s 13(1): "For successive periods of any duration, not exceeding 5 years, that the Minister may determine in each case, an
-- examination of the Pension Fund must be made by a person appointed by the Minister."
GIVEN `years in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the examination period is permitted` IF
    `years in the period` > 0 AND `years in the period` <= 5

-- s 13(2): "Despite subsection (1)", where an amendment is made (a) to the Schedule or a law in it, or (b) to a prescribed
-- superannuation scheme or its regulations, "and the amendment affects the cost of benefits payable under the law or scheme or
-- creates an initial unfunded liability", the Minister MUST appoint a person to examine and report on the Fund. (4): every report
-- "to be presented to Parliament forthwith".
GIVEN `the Schedule or a scheduled law is amended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a prescribed superannuation scheme or its regulations is amended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the amendment affects the cost of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the amendment creates an initial unfunded liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special examination must be ordered` IF
        (    `the Schedule or a scheduled law is amended`
          OR `a prescribed superannuation scheme or its regulations is amended`)
    AND (    `the amendment affects the cost of benefits`
          OR `the amendment creates an initial unfunded liability`)
